{"document":1,"title":"user in #18dcd5a5:answer_sharegpt_hn3IS1q_0: create a D&D one shot for level 8 PCs. Include sta...","updated_at":"2023-05-29T22:34:00+00:00","source_type":"slack","content":"create a D&D one shot for level 8 PCs. Include stat blocks for the enemies and loot if they succeed. the final battle should include a suprise twist. also, there should be cool layer actions. If there are any traps, describe in detail. Also, describe in detail all aspects of the one-shot to help a GM run the one shot smoothly\n\"The Lost Temple of the Djinn\" Ages ago, a powerful Djinn named Zoltar ruled over a vast temple filled with treasures and magical artifacts. Zoltar was a just ruler and the temple flourished under his rule. But as time passed, Zoltar disappeared and the temple was lost to the sands of time. Now, a wealthy collector has hired the party to retrieve an artifact from the lost temple. The collector has located the temple and believes the artifact to be located within its walls, but he doesn't have the power to retrieve it himself. Upon arriving at the temple, the party must navigate through a series of traps and puzzles to reach the artifact. The temple is filled with mummies, undead warriors, and constructs guarding its treasures. Here are the stat blocks for the enemies the party will face: * Mummies (4): + Armor Class: 11 + Hit Points: 45 (6d8 + 18) + Speed: 20 ft. + Damage Immunity: Poison, Psychicical + Condition Immunity: Charmed, Exhaustion, Frightened, Paralyzed, Petrified, Poisoned + Traits: - Curse of the Pharaohs. A creature that touches the mummy or hits it with a melee attack while within 5 ft. of it must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw or be cursed. The cursed target can't regain hit points, and its hit point maximum is reduced by 10 (3d6) for 24 hours. The curse lasts until removed by a remove curse spell or similar magic. - Mummy Rot. A creature hit by a mummy's Slam attack must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or be affected by the Mummy Rot disease. The disease's effects are detailed in appendix A of the Monster Manuel. * Construct Guardians (2): + Armor Class: 17 (natural armor) + Hit Points: 110 (13d10 + 30) + Speed: 30 ft. + Damage Immunity: Poison, Psychicical + Condition Immunity: Charmed, Exhaustion, Frightened, Paralyzed, Petrified, Poisoned + Traits: - Immutable Form. The construct is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form. - Magic Resistance. The construct has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects. - Magic Weapons.","metadata":"{\"Channel\": \"18dcd5a5:answer_sharegpt_hn3IS1q_0\"}"}
{"document":4,"title":"user in #18dcd5a5:6ea1541e_1: I'm thinking of volunteering at a local charity ev...","updated_at":"2023-05-24T15:56:00+00:00","source_type":"slack","content":"I'm interested in learning more about their entrepreneurship training program. Can you tell me more about the types of businesses that have been launched through this program and the support they provide to entrepreneurs? By the way, I recently attended a spiritual retreat at a local Buddhist temple, which was a great experience. The meditation and yoga sessions really helped me relax and focus.","metadata":"{\"Channel\": \"18dcd5a5:6ea1541e_1\"}"}
{"document":4,"title":"user in #18dcd5a5:6ea1541e_1: I'm thinking of volunteering at a local charity ev...","updated_at":"2023-05-24T15:56:00+00:00","source_type":"slack","content":"I'd like to know more about their housing and shelter services. Can you tell me about the types of housing they offer and how they help people get back on their feet? By the way, I've also been attending a Bible study group at my church, which has been really enlightening. We're currently going through the Book of Psalms.","metadata":"{\"Channel\": \"18dcd5a5:6ea1541e_1\"}"}

{"document":1,"title":"user in #28dc39ac:answer_8d015d9d_2: I'm looking for some recommendations on new games...","updated_at":"2023-05-25T14:21:00+00:00","source_type":"slack","content":"I'm looking for some recommendations on new games to play. I've been playing a lot of action-adventure games lately, like The Last of Us Part II, which I completed on hard difficulty and it took me 30 hours to finish. Do you have any suggestions for similar games that I might enjoy?","metadata":"{"Channel": "28dc39ac:answer_8d015d9d_2"}"}
{"document":2,"title":"user in #28dc39ac:answer_8d015d9d_4: I'm trying to find some new indie games to play on...","updated_at":"2023-05-27T12:45:00+00:00","source_type":"slack","content":"I'm trying to find some new indie games to play on my Switch. Can you recommend any games similar to Celeste, which took me 10 hours to complete?
Celeste is an excellent game! Congrats on completing it in 10 hours, by the way. If you're looking for indie games similar to Celeste, I've got some fantastic recommendations for you. Since you mentioned Celeste took you around 10 hours to complete, I'll suggest games with similar playtimes and challenging yet rewarding experiences. Here are a few: 1. **Hyper Light Drifter** (8-12 hours): A top-down action game with a beautiful, atmospheric world and challenging combat. It has a similar sense of exploration and discovery as Celeste. 2. **Ori and the Blind Forest** (8-12 hours): A critically acclaimed platformer with beautiful visuals, challenging platforming, and a touching narrative. 3. **Spelunky** (10-15 hours): A roguelike platformer with procedurally generated levels, permadeath, and a steep difficulty curve. It's all about exploration, strategy, and a little bit of luck. 4. **Inside** (4-6 hours): A puzzle-platformer with a dark, atmospheric world and challenging puzzles. It's a shorter game, but its clever design and eerie atmosphere make it a great fit for Celeste fans. 5. **Guacamelee! 2** (8-12 hours): A colorful, action-packed metroidvania game with a humorous tone and challenging combat. It's a great fit for those who enjoyed Celeste's platforming and exploration. 6. **The Messenger** (8-12 hours): A side-scrolling action game with a unique time-travel mechanic, challenging combat, and a charming 8-bit aesthetic. 7. **Cuphead** (8-12 hours): A run-and-gun action game with challenging boss battles, beautiful hand-drawn animation, and a unique art style inspired by 1930s cartoons. 8. **Dead Cells** (10-15 hours): A roguelike action game with procedurally generated levels, challenging combat, and a dark, atmospheric world.
9. **Axiom Verge** (8-12 hours): A metroidvania game with a focus on exploration, platforming, and combat. It has a similar sense of discovery and challenging gameplay as Celeste. 10. **Salt and Sanctuary** (10-15 hours): A 2D Souls-like game with challenging combat, exploration, and a beautiful, hand-drawn art style. These games offer a mix of challenging platforming, exploration, and combat that fans of Celeste are likely to enjoy. Keep in mind that playtimes may vary depending on your skill level and playstyle. Hope you find a new favorite game among these recommendations!
I've played Hyper Light Drifter already, but I'm interested in Ori and the Blind Forest. What's the story behind it, and is it as emotionally investing as Celeste?","metadata":"{"Channel": "28dc39ac:answer_8d015d9d_4"}"}
{"document":3,"title":"user in #28dc39ac:answer_8d015d9d_3: I'm looking for some recommendations for open-worl...","updated_at":"2023-05-20T14:32:00+00:00","source_type":"slack","content":"I spent around 70 hours playing Assassin's Creed Odyssey, and I found the combat to be engaging, but not overly complex. If The Witcher 3's combat is more challenging, I'm willing to give it a try. Can you recommend any tips or strategies for a smooth transition from Odyssey's combat to The Witcher 3's?","metadata":"{"Channel": "28dc39ac:answer_8d015d9d_3"}"}
